{"agent_id":"pp3g-xVYS-research-only-investigation-425-deferred-part-2-of","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T19:19:37.231374406Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"51afdc1a-bbd7-4e47-88b1-d9f03409877e","comment_uuid":"1d9bebcc-8507-4e6c-a418-a2a38f86d5c1","author":"pp3g-xVYS-research-only-investigation-425-deferred-part-2-of","content":"Plan: (1) Inspect live resolved config on both surfaces: opencode debug config + opencode debug agent orchestrator (S2 fork 1.18.13-pp3g) and opencode2 debug config/agents (S1 v2 beta) to capture actual permission resolution. (2) Read permission matcher source in fork/opencode-src: packages/opencode/src/permission/index.ts (evaluate/Wildcard/fromConfig/disabled/visibleTools), packages/core/src/util/wildcard, schema/permission.ts, tool registry + session Prompt where Permission.ask is called to trace native vs MCP tool permission strings. (3) Read plugins/orchestrator-guard.ts block list behavior + any v2-side equivalent searched via glob/grep. (4) Where behavior cannot be read from source, probe headless: create scratch dir under /tmp/opencode/425-probe and attempt filesystem_read_text_file + filesystem_write_file as orchestrator-type agent via opencode run --agent orchestrator to observe allow/deny/ask. (5) Synthesize answers to Q1-Q4 with WHY/WHAT/HOW-CERTAIN/WHAT-NOT-TESTED per claim and recommend exact frontmatter keys. No repo file changes; scratch only under /tmp/opencode.","created_at":"2026-08-23T19:19:37.224652653Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:PEhbr63L0EG90FNYmzfxGdJ97wr3fudWUbtjj02d2lI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgIjCHG5o33kWB2JEhe9xdEU8KEnFd3GVZE+NzNCbfc+kAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABANOsyxuVo+uVjgzFnI19HsgFu/9Js50KSISOymcLfDnnZDKBKcmhyCJmc0a1DAAZZrWSp7BjKNptxMWyeRXn5DQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:PEhbr63L0EG90FNYmzfxGdJ97wr3fudWUbtjj02d2lI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgIjCHG5o33kWB2JEhe9xdEU8KEnFd3GVZE+